  "preamble": "Affrication of the retroflex stop [ʈ] to the retroflex affricate [ʈʂ]. In the history of Chinese, the Middle Chinese retroflex stop series (the 知 zhī initials) merged with the retroflex affricates in most Mandarin varieties, so that Middle Chinese ʈ- words are now pronounced with zh [ʈʂ]; old-style Changsha Xiang shows the same outcome, while Wu, Gan and Hakka went on to plain [ts] or [tɕ] and Min kept the stop as [t].",
